  "subject": {
    "id": "contract-compiler-steady-state-evidence-gate",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Repair steady-state evidence checks and bind CC-002 checkpoint lineage.",
  "why": "CC-D01 evidence is an immutable historical report, while verify-evidence compares its artifact records with the current mutable source snapshot before sealing. Repeating that pre-seal command in steady-state CI and release became invalid when a later governed document revision changed the protocol graph. The workflows retain ledger tests and ledger check, which validate the append-only history and latest document revisions. A structural regression test prevents either workflow from revalidating retained overseer evidence. This prerequisite does not revise CC-D01 evidence. It also resolves the CC-002 card's incompatible range wording: an intervening overseer prerequisite may be the final materialization base, while final artifacts and evidence must bind the three already-committed governed worker checkpoints explicitly."
}
